# Automatic optimization (cronjob)
ffmpeg_auto_legend = Automatic optimization
ffmpeg_auto_intro = New videos are automatically scaled down to a standard size and prepared for the web (H.264, fast start: plays instantly in the browser). The original is replaced – file name, title and all metadata are kept. It is only replaced if the file gets smaller or the original does not play reliably in browsers; if only fast start is missing, the file is rearranged losslessly. Videos are never scaled up. One video at a time: right after the upload and then every 10 minutes via cronjob.
ffmpeg_auto_enabled = Optimize videos automatically
ffmpeg_auto_preset = Standard size
ffmpeg_auto_preset_1080p = Full HD – at most 1920 × 1080 (recommended)
ffmpeg_auto_preset_720p = HD – at most 1280 × 720 (smaller files)
ffmpeg_auto_preset_480p = Small – at most 854 × 480 (e.g. background videos)
ffmpeg_auto_preset_help = Applies to landscape and portrait (portrait Full HD: 1080 × 1920). Smaller videos are only converted if their format or bitrate is not suitable for the web.
ffmpeg_auto_scope = Which videos?
ffmpeg_auto_scope_new = Only videos uploaded after switching it on
ffmpeg_auto_scope_all = All existing videos in the media pool as well
ffmpeg_auto_status_running = Running: {0} ({1} %)
ffmpeg_auto_status_pending = Still to check: {0} video(s)
ffmpeg_auto_cronjob_link = Show cronjob "FFmpeg: optimize videos automatically"
ffmpeg_auto_no_cronjob_addon = The "Cronjob" add-on is not installed: videos are only optimized right after the upload. Alternatively run the console command from a system cronjob.
ffmpeg_auto_console_hint = Console: "php redaxo/bin/console ffmpeg:optimize --wait" processes all waiting videos one after another.
ffmpeg_auto_cronjob_name = FFmpeg: optimize videos automatically
ffmpeg_auto_cronjob_description = Scales new videos in the media pool down to the standard size and processes queued jobs (settings in Media pool → Video tools → Settings).
config_always = Always included: H.264 with AAC audio (plays in every browser), browser-compatible colour format, fast start (the video starts instantly). Videos are never scaled up, portrait stays portrait.
ffmpeg_option_size = Size
ffmpeg_option_size_help = At most this size – portrait accordingly (Full HD: at most 1080 × 1920). Smaller videos stay as they are.
ffmpeg_option_quality = Quality
ffmpeg_option_quality_help = "Balanced" is hard to tell apart from the source. "High" for archive and close-ups, "Small file" for long and background videos.
ffmpeg_option_audio = Audio
ffmpeg_option_audio_help = "Normalize loudness" brings quiet and loud videos to the same level (−16 LUFS). "Remove" e.g. for background videos – saves space.
ffmpeg_size_original = Original size
ffmpeg_size_1080p = Full HD – at most 1920 × 1080
ffmpeg_size_720p = HD – at most 1280 × 720
ffmpeg_size_480p = Small – at most 854 × 480
ffmpeg_size_360p = Very small – at most 640 × 360
ffmpeg_quality_high = High (larger file)
ffmpeg_quality_balanced = Balanced (recommended)
ffmpeg_quality_small = Small file
